    {
      "id": "CPL-01",
      "title": "Character reductions for the plus eigenspace",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-plus-count",
      "statement": "For a large host, odd ℓ and 1≤e<t, use the characters of the quotient that have parity (−1)^e. The exterior reduction is lossless when ℓ does not divide the subgroup index. The integral reduction for arbitrary odd ℓ adds one loss per character. The cases I,Z,II,III outside Bχ and II,IV,V inside it exhaust the permitted inputs.",
      "hypotheses": "Host index n≥2; auxiliary primes q≡3 mod 8, d≡7 mod 16, gcd(qd,Q)=1; Host.Big t; 1≤e<t; E a CM IsChiField at the host level. The coefficient DVR is finite over ℤ_ℓ and has enough roots of unity for φ(N). Algebraic closures and local data are part of the quantifiers.",
